From ed09a29734555ac99dfa8dcee8dc52878784096a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Connor Avila <Connoravila@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 16:15:01 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 02/10] sign_psbt: fail on anti-exfil fields on every transport

Requests for anti-exfil signing carry host randomness in unknown input
fields, and were signed in the ordinary way, with the fields kept in the
result. Over QR and USB storage that result is displayed or written out.
Detect the fields from the decoded key type on the parsed keys, since the
shortest form of the type is not enforced when parsing, and reject the
request before any signing.
---
